# Nougat extraction stub

This file exists for pipeline uniformity. Nougat OCR was NOT run for this
paper because:

- The source PDF (`../paper.pdf`) is a text-native open-access publication
  from Frontiers in Medicine; text is directly extractable via `pdftotext`.
- No scanned-page or figure-only OCR was needed for the replication work.
- The paper's Methods §2.2, Eq. 1, Table 1, and Table 2 — the four
  content blocks the replication depends on — were read directly from the
  paper by the human/subagent reviewer.

If a full Nougat extraction is later required (e.g., for downstream corpus
indexing or LaTeX-clean equation extraction), run:

```
nougat ../paper.pdf --out . --model 0.1.0-base
```

expected output: `paper.mmd` (Markdown+math) here.

## What was actually used from the paper
- Methods §2.2 (DSB scoring rule; positional-source specification)
- Eq. 1 (Humm & Charlton 1989 lethal-damage formula)
- Table 1 (DSB/decay per nuclide at 0.25 nm and 1.15 nm)
- Table 2 (initial activity A and atoms/cell N₀)
- Refs 27, 34 (chromatin geometry; earlier 2020 DBSCAN paper — cited to
  disambiguate the triage-tag error)

Everything else in the paper (introduction, discussion, clinical context)
was read but not machine-extracted.
